    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0305" n="201" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg201"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3928: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-03T23:00:00-05:00">February 3, 1932—11
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 3, 9 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Department approves your joining your colleagues in making representations
                        in the sense indicated.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Department has already on basis of your February 3, 2 a.m. and other data
                        instructed Ambassador Tokyo to make a fourth set of representations on this
                            subject.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d221-f1"/> British Government had
                        instructed British Ambassador Tokyo to make such representations and had
                        suggested to French and Italian Governments they take similar action.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Inform Nanking and Legation.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d221-f1" n="47" xml:id="d221-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 37, February 3, 5 p.m., to the Ambassador in Japan, <ref
                        target="frus1931-41v01#pg_179"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, p. 179</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
